+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "toolChoice: 'required',",
+  "cause": "The refundAgent sets toolChoice to 'required', which forces the model to emit a tool call on every turn, so after approveRefund is declined it cannot produce a final text reply and instead re-requests approval, reworks the order, or runs out of tool iterations.",
+  "evidence": "Reproduced by running refundAgent with a declined approval: before the fix the turn failed with 'ABORTED: Exceeded maximum tool call iterations (6)'; after changing it to toolChoice: 'auto' the same decline ends with finishReason 'stop' and a reply to the customer saying the refund was not approved because of a duplicate claim (repeated twice), and an approved run still issues the refund."
+}
